{
  "what": "the 30 shipped wave-2 actors re-evaluated with the CLEAN Tier 1 reference as input",
  "question": "Tier 1 permits the clean multi-view trajectory as input. Does feeding it to the policies we already have beat the entry we submitted, which was driven by the noisy Tier 2 input?",
  "answer": "No, decisively: mean kit AUC falls from 0.46523 to 0.28937 and SP-SR from 0.667 to 0.133. Only 2 of 30 clips improved.",
  "why": "Each actor was trained against one specific reference (bridge_v1, or its arm's cleaned tree). Swapping the reference at evaluation time is a distribution shift, not an upgrade: the policy learned to track the trajectory it saw, so a cleaner but different one puts it off-policy. That is a property of these actors, not of the input, and it is the argument for fine-tuning (brev/patch_warm_start.py) rather than swapping the reference cold.",
  "one_variable": "Same actors, same z-drop picks, same evaluator build, same scorer; only the reference parquet differs. Every clip's rigid-frame check came out at or below 1.7e-05 cm and 5e-06 deg, so these numbers are not a frame artefact.",
  "control_still_owed": "a 2-clip Tier 2-input control (e00, e03) through this same patched eval image, expecting the shipped 0.5178 and 0.7806; needs a box (~$0.7) and would rule out the eval image itself as the cause.",
  "box": "v2d-t1eval-01, massedcompute_A6000_plus, eval only, no training, ~$0.6 over four attempts",
  "means_over_30_clips": {
    "add_auc": 0.28937,
    "spider_sr": 0.13333,
    "maniptrans_sr": 0.03333,
    "mppe_cm": 48.778
  },
